# Boolean fit checks — rendered by gate.sh, never printed or sliced.
# Each `empty` proof is real volume clearance, not a surface kiss, and each
# has a control that must interfere or the proof is proving nothing.
#
# joint-fit: the production key inside the production socket, posed as
#   joined (end faces joint_gap apart). Zero facets = joint_clear (0.2 mm per
#   face) of air all round the drafted dovetail.
# joint-fit-ctrl: the same pair with the socket cut at -0.15 mm clearance —
#   0.15 mm of interference on every flank.
joint-fit         empty
joint-fit-ctrl    interferes
# spindle-fit: the spindle laid in its saddle pockets, against the whole
#   cradle. Zero facets = it seats (0.3 mm radial, 0.4 mm at each end).
# spindle-fit-ctrl: the hub grown 1.2 mm on diameter — twice the saddle
#   clearance — must jam in the pockets.
spindle-fit       empty
spindle-fit-ctrl  interferes
# roll-fit: two rolls at the brief's maximum (62 mm outer, 25.4 mm core,
#   19 mm wide) on the spindle in the cradle. Zero facets = they clear the
#   floor, both walls, the gate and the spindle flange.
# roll-fit-ctrl: rolls 8 mm larger, which must hit the floor.
roll-fit          empty
roll-fit-ctrl     interferes
